          <change when="2024-07-18T08:59:39-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/G.%20Papaioannou">Submit - Fr.B VI 13 ind(ictione) -&gt; indict(ione). -ict- is visible in both the plate (Taf. 23) and the online image. This is the second instance of indict(ion-) in Italian papyri (and in Latin papyri in  general), the other one being P.Ital. I 18+19 17 indict(ione). P.Ital. I 7 7 indict(ione) is another instance but the document is preserved on an inscription. ind(iction-) is the preferred mode of abbreviation in papyri.&#xD;
I cannot find the Meta tab to add a link to the BnF images: https://archivesetmanuscrits.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/cc62376f.</change>
